          "text": "The agent controls a real Chrome or Chromium through the agent-browser CLI: it opens pages, clicks, fills forms and takes screenshots. Rather than raw HTML, it reads each page as an accessibility snapshot with short element references, which keeps pages cheap in tokens. The skill itself is only a stub that tells the agent to load the full guide from the installed CLI, so the instructions always match the version you have. Extra guides cover Electron desktop apps such as VS Code, Slack or Figma, exploratory QA, and cloud browsers in Vercel Sandbox or AWS.",
