          "text": "A one-time step before generating images or videos of a real person. The agent asks for a one-word name and 5 to 20 photos of the face from varied angles and lighting, and trains the Soul for still images by default, or for cinematic shots and video if that's what you'll use it for. Training takes minutes; the agent waits without status chatter and tells you when the Soul is ready. From then on, higgsfield-generate can use it in any generation. It can also list the Souls you already have. You don't need it for a one-off face swap from a single photo, or for an invented character with no real face to learn: higgsfield-generate handles both directly.",
