          "text": "You give it a product photo, or a clear enough description, and the agent picks one of four ready-made sets: the main image alone, the main image plus 5 secondary images, the main image plus 7 \"A+\" sections (Amazon's term for the richer content further down a product page), or all 13 images together. It can also make single images, such as an infographic, several angles, a detail shot, a lifestyle shot, what's in the box, or an A+ section on features or how to use the product. The skill doesn't name particular marketplaces. Higgsfield keeps the marketplace rules and prompt templates on its side, so the agent never writes image prompts itself. It asks at most one confirmation question, then replies with the image links only.",
