      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Maps a deep-learning research repo's entry points, configs and suspicious code patterns, read-only.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you want to understand a deep-learning research repo before changing it, without running anything heavy"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "maps the model structure, the training, inference and evaluation entry points and how configs connect, and points out where changes could plug in"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "an analysis_outputs/ folder with a summary, a risks file and a machine-readable status"
            },
            {
              "label": "Doesn't",
              "text": "patch code, launch heavy jobs, or call a suspicious pattern a confirmed bug"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike",
              "text": "repo-intake-and-plan, which picks a README command to reproduce, it explains the code itself"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A read-only skill from RigorPilot, a set of skills that reproduces deep-learning research code from its README. It looks for the likely training, inference and evaluation entry points, summarizes how configs and scripts are laid out, and suggests insertion points, the places where a new module or change would plug in, conservatively. Patterns that look wrong, checked against a research-pitfall checklist that ships with the repo's main skill, ai-research-reproduction, are reported as heuristics to review, not as bugs. It may run lightweight static inspection helpers and writes only its own report files: it never patches the repository's code or starts heavy training or evaluation. The main skill calls it only when a repo's structure needs clarifying, and ai-research-explore usually uses it to understand a repo before trying ideas; on its own, it fits the moment before you plan changes to someone else's research code.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/lllllllama/rigorpilot-skills/tree/fb3ccdf5aa64b1fa5b1d0463e666a8bc8bc26e01/skills/analyze-project"
        },
        "tags": [
          "category:science",
          "type:workflow",
          "effect:local",
          "needs:none",
          "by:community",
          "stack:python",
          "ml-research",
          "architecture",
          "code-review"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lllllllama/rigorpilot-skills/skills/ai-research-reproduction",
      "name": "ai-research-reproduction",
      "skills.sh": {
        "url": "https://skills.sh/lllllllama/rigorpilot-skills/ai-research-reproduction",
        "installs": 349791,
        "weeklyInstalls": [51, 41, 40, 51, 3509, 10924, 11042, 8762],
        "firstSeen": "2026-04-04"
      },
      "skillMd": {
        "version": "fb3ccdf5aa64b1fa5b1d0463e666a8bc8bc26e01",
        "updated": "2026-11-06",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Reproduces a deep-learning repo from its README through the smallest documented run, and records the evidence.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you want an agent to run a deep-learning research repo from its README and record honestly what worked"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "lists the README's commands, picks the smallest trustworthy one, usually inference or evaluation, runs it through bundled scripts and verifies the evidence"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "a repro_outputs/ folder: summary, exact commands, log, status, notes on anything that changes the science, and the README annotated section by section"
            },
            {
              "label": "Stops for you",
              "text": "before full training, and before changing a dataset, split, checkpoint, preprocessing step, metric, loss or the model's meaning"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Python 3.11+ and Git"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike",
              "text": "ai-research-explore, which tries new ideas on a working baseline, it only runs what the README documents, calling the repo's step skills as needed"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The main skill of RigorPilot. For a target it prefers documented inference, then evaluation, then a training startup check, and full training only after you confirm. Its fast path is three calls to its orchestrator script: a plan that lists the README's commands as numbered candidates with a fingerprint of that list, a run of the chosen candidate that fails if the list has changed since, and a check of the evidence. The README is the authority: repo files only clarify it, and if the paper disagrees, the conflict is recorded and paper-context-resolver answers just that question. It uses minimal-run-and-audit for inference and evaluation, run-train for training, and analyze-project only when the repo's structure is unclear. Fixes try arguments, environment variables, paths and dependency versions before code; code edits go on a repro/ branch and into PATCHES.md, and avoid touching architecture, training logic or losses. A run that finishes isn't called a match: that verdict needs expected metrics and a tolerance. The annotated README keeps the original byte for byte outside its inserted blocks, and can also be written beside the original as RIGORPILOT_README.md. Once it delivers the result it stops, without starting optional stages on its own.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/lllllllama/rigorpilot-skills/tree/fb3ccdf5aa64b1fa5b1d0463e666a8bc8bc26e01/skills/ai-research-reproduction"
        },
        "tags": [
          "category:science",
          "type:workflow",
          "effect:local",
          "needs:none",
          "by:community",
          "stack:python",
          "ml-research",
          "verification"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lllllllama/rigorpilot-skills/skills/safe-debug",
      "name": "safe-debug",
      "skills.sh": {
        "url": "https://skills.sh/lllllllama/rigorpilot-skills/safe-debug",
        "installs": 349460,
        "weeklyInstalls": [45, 34, 41, 42, 3506, 10920, 11044, 8761],
