        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Plans and ranks small exploratory runs, such as subset checks and short sweeps, on top of a research baseline.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you've authorized quick experiments on a research baseline: small-subset checks, short training probes, batch sweeps, idle-GPU searches or transfer-learning trials"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "plans candidate runs from the variants, subset sizes and step counts you set, ranks them by cost, chance of success and expected gain, and trims them to budget"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "an explore_outputs/ folder ranking the runs, with what changed and where a comparison isn't fair"
            },
            {
              "label": "Hands off",
              "text": "the actual runs to minimal-run-and-audit or run-train"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike run-train",
              "text": "its results are labeled candidate evidence, never trusted or state-of-the-art results"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The run step of RigorPilot's exploration lane, which tries new ideas on top of a reproduced baseline, kept apart from the reproduction itself. It works only when you explicitly ask for exploration. You describe the grid of variants to try, the subset sizes and short-run step counts, and optionally how to weigh cost, chance of success and expected gain; the default weights stay conservative. A bundled planner scores the candidates and cuts them to your limits on variants and short runs. Small, short checks come before heavier ones, and once runs have executed, ranking switches from these estimates to measured results, ordered by the metric you named. Experiment state stays separate from the trusted baseline, results are summarized for you to review, and nothing moves into the trusted lane automatically. It doesn't rewrite training logic.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/lllllllama/rigorpilot-skills/tree/fb3ccdf5aa64b1fa5b1d0463e666a8bc8bc26e01/skills/explore-run"
        },
        "tags": [
