      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Suggests marketing ideas for a SaaS product from a library of 139, matched to your stage and budget.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you're stuck on how to market a SaaS or software product and want ideas that fit where you are"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "asks about your product, audience, stage and resources, then picks 3 to 5 ideas from a library of 139"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "each idea with why it fits, the first 2 or 3 steps, what success looks like, and the time, budget and skills it takes"
            },
            {
              "label": "Covers",
              "text": "content and SEO, free tools, paid ads, community, email, partnerships, events, launches, product-led growth, PR and more"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike marketing-plan",
              "text": "from the same repo, it suggests standalone ideas rather than a full plan"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A library of 139 marketing ideas for software products, in 17 categories from content and SEO to developer relations and international expansion, with the full list and descriptions in a reference file. It reads your product marketing context if you have it (a shared file on your product, audience and positioning that the repo's product-marketing skill writes) first, then asks only what's missing: your stage and main goal, budget and team size, what you've tried, and competitor tactics you admire. Shortlists match ideas to stage (waitlist referrals before launch, partnerships and events during growth), budget (content and community for free, conferences for big budgets), timeline, and goals such as fast leads, authority, low-budget growth, product-led growth or enterprise sales. Guerrilla marketing gets its own deep dive with a case library. For carrying out a channel, it points to the repo's other skills, such as programmatic-seo, emails or referrals.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/coreyhaines31/marketingskills/tree/96798cf38736ecdba015a1d2b0521b0c8f8f41dd/skills/marketing-ideas"
