            {
              "label": "Websites",
              "text": "get their own brand and no AI features; you're always asked animated or not, and animated, the recommended pick, scrolls through one generated film of about 15 seconds"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "the higgsfield CLI, which it installs if missing, a Higgsfield account, and git and bun"
            },
            {
              "label": "Overrides",
              "text": "your other web-design skills: it tells the agent not to look for or follow them"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Higgsfield, an AI image, video and audio generation platform, also hosts sites, and this skill drives its builder to create, edit and deploy them. Each product is a React app rendered on the server in one Cloudflare Worker, with optional storage. The first question settles the type: a website, independent of Higgsfield; an app, whose users sign in with Higgsfield and generate media on their own credits, built with Higgsfield's Quanta design system; or a game, single or multiplayer rooms where the game logic is six functions and the platform runs the networking. The same question asks whether to publish to Higgsfield's community feed when done. Websites then follow fixed phases: concept, reference boards, generated assets, a build matched to the boards, a motion pass, cover and share text, checks, then deploy. Every build gets a generated cover image without asking; a cover video costs credits, so it is only offered. Game art, textures, 3D animation and audio are covered too. The agent edits code locally, talks to you in product terms rather than developer ones, replies in your language and returns the live URL with a one-line summary.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/higgsfield-ai/skills/tree/27000402070db19d958789d05b3b52b6f4718d7c/higgsfield-websites"
