        "url": "https://skills.sh/coreyhaines31/marketingskills/social",
        "installs": 93335,
        "weeklyInstalls": [2921, 2694, 2904, 3492, 3994, 4335, 4594, 5223],
        "firstSeen": "2026-05-14"
      },
      "skillMd": {
        "version": "96798cf38736ecdba015a1d2b0521b0c8f8f41dd",
        "updated": "2026-11-06",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Writes and plans social media posts for LinkedIn, X, Instagram, TikTok and Facebook, from hooks and carousels to repurposing, calendars and short-form video scripts.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you need posts, a content calendar or ideas for what to post, or want to turn a blog post or podcast into social content"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "builds 3-5 content pillars, writes hooks and posts per platform, and cuts long content into standalone pieces"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "post drafts, carousel slide plans, a weekly calendar, and short video scripts timed second by second"
            },
            {
              "label": "Bans",
              "text": "AI tells such as \"it's not X, it's Y\", one-line-per-sentence \"broetry\", engagement bait and emoji bullets"
            },
            {
              "label": "Can publish",
              "text": "through a connected scheduling tool such as Typefully or Buffer, as drafts first and never without your go-ahead"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Social content with storytelling first: platform tactics only amplify a good story. It reads your product marketing context if you have it (a shared file on your product, audience and positioning that the repo's product-marketing skill writes), then asks about goals, audience, brand voice and how much time you have. A quick reference gives each platform's audience, posting frequency and main format, with deeper references on each platform, character limits, and how X ranks its For You feed. Hooks come in curiosity, story, value and contrarian shapes, to be filled with a specific fact or story. Repurposing pulls 5-10 self-contained moments from a blog post, podcast, webinar or newsletter and adapts each to a platform. It also sets a 30-minute daily engagement routine, a weekly review of top and bottom posts, a method for studying what works for top creators in your niche, and short-form video structures in which the visual, spoken and on-screen hooks all land in the first second. A listening reference helps pick which posts to comment on and track brand mentions.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/coreyhaines31/marketingskills/tree/96798cf38736ecdba015a1d2b0521b0c8f8f41dd/skills/social"
