      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Extracts an existing website's design system into a DESIGN.md, or collects its logo, colors, fonts and messaging, using Firecrawl.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you want to build UI that matches a reference website, document its design patterns, or match a slide or proposal to a company's brand"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "scrapes the site's branding data, text and images with Firecrawl, downloads a full-page screenshot and inspects it before describing the look"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "a DESIGN.md of tokens, typography, spacing, components, section order and implementation guidance, tied to evidence; or a compact asset reference for a document"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "the Firecrawl CLI and a Firecrawl API key"
            },
            {
              "label": "Won't",
              "text": "promise a pixel-perfect copy, invent a new brand, or imply you have rights to the site's logos, images or copy"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Its design-system mode starts from the URL you give, or finds the official site when you only name a company, and captures one representative page with Firecrawl's branding, Markdown and image formats plus a full-page screenshot. The screenshot comes back as an expiring link, so the agent downloads it into .firecrawl/ and looks at the actual pixels before making visual claims, using HTML or stylesheets to fill in missing fonts or tokens. It extracts color roles, typography, spacing, containers, borders, shadows, component patterns, section order and how images are treated, and keeps extracted values, visual estimates and its own suggestions apart. A desktop screenshot isn't taken as evidence of mobile layout, hover states or animation. DESIGN.md lists source URLs, capture context, the screenshot, tokens, components, image references, guidance adapted to your stack when you name one, and unresolved details, saved as a file when the agent can. If you only need a logo, palette, fonts or homepage messaging for a document, it skips the design-system report and returns a short asset reference instead.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/firecrawl/firecrawl-workflows/tree/d2a986240f9d786ae54fc33fcfd9ad37308e9cc3/skills/firecrawl-website-design-clone"
