        "updated": "2026-11-06",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Picks the Firecrawl workflow skill that fits your request, such as research, SEO audits, QA or lead lists, with a generic fallback process.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you want a finished, sourced deliverable from the web, such as a report, audit or lead list, and don't know which Firecrawl workflow fits"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "routes the request to one of Firecrawl's workflow skills, or follows a generic process when none fits"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "whatever the chosen workflow produces; from the fallback, a summary, the evidence used, the analysis, next steps and rerun inputs"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "the other Firecrawl workflow skills, the Firecrawl CLI and a Firecrawl API key"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike the firecrawl skill",
              "text": "that one gives the agent Firecrawl's commands for any web task, from search to crawling; this one picks a workflow that ends in a finished deliverable"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The entry point of Firecrawl's workflow skills. It lists which workflow handles what: finding new prospects, researching named people and companies, published business contacts, current job openings, fantasy-sports decisions, a website's brand assets or design system, literature reviews, web research reports, SEO audits, live-site QA, competitor monitoring, company directories, dashboard metrics, knowledge bases, docs-portal exports, market research, product walkthroughs and shopping research. Questions about official documentation go to firecrawl-developer-index, a skill installed with the Firecrawl CLI. It infers the inputs and asks at most three short questions, only when something missing blocks the work. When no workflow fits, it gathers evidence with Firecrawl, keeps sources traceable, runs independent units such as one competitor or one URL in parallel subagents where available, and writes a deliverable with a summary, the evidence base, the analysis, recommendations and a block of inputs for rerunning it, so the pattern could become a new skill; a checklist for writing such skills comes with it. Focused workflows keep their own outputs: a contact card or fantasy pick doesn't turn into a research report.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/firecrawl/firecrawl-workflows/tree/d2a986240f9d786ae54fc33fcfd9ad37308e9cc3/skills/firecrawl-workflows"
        },
        "tags": [
          "category:skill-tools",
          "type:router",
          "effect:none",
          "needs:cli",
          "needs:account",
          "by:official",
          "stack:firecrawl",
          "skill-discovery",
          "research",
          "flag:mirror"
        ],
        "note": "Routes each request to the other Firecrawl workflow skills, so it needs them installed; alone, only its short generic process is left."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "firecrawl/firecrawl-workflows/skills/firecrawl-knowledge-base",
      "name": "firecrawl-knowledge-base",
      "skills.sh": {
        "url": "https://skills.sh/firecrawl/firecrawl-workflows/firecrawl-knowledge-base",
        "installs": 32800,
        "weeklyInstalls": [272, 295, 267, 237, 175, 190, 127, 152],
        "firstSeen": "2026-05-15"
      },
      "skillMd": {
        "version": "d2a986240f9d786ae54fc33fcfd9ad37308e9cc3",
        "updated": "2026-11-06",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Turns websites or topics into organized, LLM-ready Markdown with Firecrawl: reference docs, RAG chunks, training data or docs mirrors.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you want web docs or a topic collected as local files for reference, retrieval by an AI (RAG), fine-tuning or a Markdown mirror of a docs site"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "maps documentation sites or searches a topic with Firecrawl, scrapes pages into Markdown with code and tables kept, and files them by host and path"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "files under .firecrawl/ plus, depending on the goal, sources.json, chunk files and a manifest, or training JSONL, and a summary of coverage"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "the Firecrawl CLI and a Firecrawl API key"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike firecrawl-knowledge-ingest",
              "text": "that one clicks through JavaScript-heavy or login-gated docs portals in a browser; this one maps and scrapes pages"
            }
          ],
          "text": "It turns URLs or topics into content an AI model can use. You say the source and the goal, and it picks one of four outputs: reference (Markdown files with an index.md and sources.json), RAG (Markdown plus chunk files and a manifest.json, for retrieval-augmented generation, where a model looks up passages before answering), training (the scraped files plus training-data.jsonl and its metadata, for fine-tuning) or a docs mirror (a complete Markdown copy with a table of contents). For documentation sites it lists the site's URLs first; for topics it searches. Pages are saved as .firecrawl/<host>/<path>/index.md, with navigation boilerplate removed where possible, code examples and formatting kept, and source URLs in each file's metadata. It asks up to three questions only when the source, goal or training format is unclear. Work can be split across subagents by docs section or source type. It ends with a summary of what was collected, the file structure, coverage counts, usage notes and rerun inputs.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/firecrawl/firecrawl-workflows/tree/d2a986240f9d786ae54fc33fcfd9ad37308e9cc3/skills/firecrawl-knowledge-base"
        },
        "tags": [
          "category:browser",
          "type:workflow",
          "needs:cli",
          "needs:account",
          "by:official",
          "stack:firecrawl",
          "effect:local",
          "scraping",
          "flag:mirror"
        ]
      }
    },
