            {
              "label": "Won't",
              "text": "bypass access controls; when a login has expired it asks you to sign in again"
            }
          ],
          "text": "It extracts the metrics visible on dashboards you can legitimately access. It infers the URLs, metrics, date range and output format, asking up to three questions only when blocked, such as whether a dashboard needs a signed-in profile. In Firecrawl's browser it opens each dashboard, sets or checks the date range, reads KPI cards, tables and labels, clicks tabs, expands sections and scrolls tables, and uses export or download buttons only when appropriate and allowed. It records actual numbers rather than chart labels and says when a chart can't be read precisely. Where the agent can run subagents, it can split the work by platform or metric category. JSON output has a set shape: report time, date range, dashboards, metrics, tables, exports and a summary.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/firecrawl/firecrawl-workflows/tree/d2a986240f9d786ae54fc33fcfd9ad37308e9cc3/skills/firecrawl-dashboard-reporting"
