        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Builds a ranked, sourced list of prospects or target accounts matching your criteria from Firecrawl's people and company data providers.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you want a lead list: people by role, seniority, company, industry, size, location or technology, or companies that fit your criteria"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "finds a people or company provider in Alexandria, Firecrawl's catalog of data tools, checks which filters it supports, searches, deduplicates, ranks and fills missing fields"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "a ranked table or CSV of name, title, company, size, location, LinkedIn URL, work email only if asked, why each fits, and sources"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "the Firecrawl CLI and a Firecrawl API key; some providers need an organization admin to accept their terms in the Firecrawl dashboard"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike firecrawl-lead-research",
              "text": "that one enriches people and companies you already have; this one finds new ones"
            },
            {
              "label": "Won't",
              "text": "guess emails or profile URLs, ask for personal emails or phone numbers, create CRM records or send outreach"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Profile and contact fields come only from the data providers. The web is used just to find candidates for criteria only it shows, such as a recent news item or an event's speaker list, which are then looked up through the providers. When company criteria apply, it finds matching companies first, then searches for people at their domains, following pagination until it reaches your count or the results run out. It skips results that failed, and treats a masked surname or a flag that an email exists as incomplete until enriched. It never relaxes a required filter to reach the count, and ends with how many people and companies it found, the total the provider reported, any shortfall and the criteria it couldn't confirm. If you name a directory or database, it extracts that first, using Firecrawl's interact command for filters and pagination; a plain export of a company directory goes to firecrawl-company-directories instead. Run the same search again later and it returns only new prospects, plus anyone who changed role or employer.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/firecrawl/firecrawl-workflows/tree/d2a986240f9d786ae54fc33fcfd9ad37308e9cc3/skills/firecrawl-lead-gen"
