            }
          ],
          "text": "Fields come only from the data providers. The web adds context such as news or talks but never fills a field a provider didn't return, and empty fields are named as missing. For a list or CSV it keeps every input column, row and row order, adds the requested fields plus a match status (matched, not found or error) and sources, and uses a provider's bulk lookup when there is one. Masked values and flags that an email exists don't count as data. Asked to refresh a list it enriched before, it runs again and reports only what changed, such as new titles, employers, headcount or funding. A meeting brief follows a guide that comes with the skill: it enriches the company and each attendee, searches for dated news, funding, launches and hiring, and finds their talks or posts. It then sets out what the company sells, each attendee's role, recent activity newest first, talking points and likely priorities marked as hypotheses. It sticks to professional context and collects no private details.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/firecrawl/firecrawl-workflows/tree/d2a986240f9d786ae54fc33fcfd9ad37308e9cc3/skills/firecrawl-lead-research"
