      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Tests a live website with Firecrawl's browser and writes a QA report of broken links, forms, mobile layout, performance and errors.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you want a pre-launch check, a bug hunt or confirmation that a deployed site works"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "maps the site's pages, then tests links, forms, content, layouts, error states or performance in Firecrawl's browser, with testers that can run as parallel subagents"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "a QA report: a health score out of 10, critical, major and minor issues, steps to reproduce the serious ones, what works well, pages tested and rerun inputs"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "the Firecrawl CLI and a Firecrawl API key; credentials if you want protected flows tested"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike webapp-testing",
              "text": "it tests a deployed site through Firecrawl's browser; Anthropic's webapp-testing writes Playwright scripts against an app on your machine"
            }
          ],
          "text": "You give a URL and optionally a focus: full, forms, navigation, responsive or performance. Each focus splits into four testers. A full run covers navigation and links, forms and interactions, content and visuals, and error states; a forms run covers discovery, the happy path, edge cases and validation; navigation covers the sitemap, menus, links and routing; responsive covers desktop, tablet, mobile and interaction; performance covers page load, assets, content efficiency and comparison. Each tester returns severity, URL, description, evidence and steps to reproduce. The report merges duplicate findings across testers and leaves out speculative bugs without evidence. The result is a report, not fixes.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/firecrawl/firecrawl-workflows/tree/d2a986240f9d786ae54fc33fcfd9ad37308e9cc3/skills/firecrawl-qa"
