        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Optimizes a React Native app's performance with lint and code sweeps, then profiling the running app to find and fix the worst bottlenecks.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "a React Native app feels slow, janky or slow to start, and you want it measurably faster"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "sweeps the code with an ESLint performance ruleset and a judgment checklist, has subagents fix the findings, then profiles key flows and fixes the worst offenders"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "code fixes checked against a target metric, re-profiled after each architectural change, then a pass over every screen for errors the fixes introduced"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "the Argent MCP server, subagents, argent-react-native-profiler, which it loads for profiling, and argent-device-interact for navigating screens"
            },
            {
              "label": "Installs",
              "text": "any ESLint plugins the ruleset needs that your project lacks; the extra rules apply for that one run"
            },
            {
              "label": "Skips",
              "text": "memoization fixes when the project uses React Compiler, except for components the compiler leaves out"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Software Mansion's entry point for performance work on a React Native app, run through Argent, their MCP server that lets the agent control simulators, emulators and devices. Its rule is to measure first: set a target metric and threshold, fix the top offender, re-measure honestly, and check a fix with debugger-evaluate before committing it. It works through a four-phase checklist. Phase 1 runs ESLint over the source with React Native performance rules, such as no inline styles or index keys, and sends subagents to fix the results, one per file. Phase 2 reviews areas that need judgment, such as memoization, lists, animations, fetch waterfalls, effect cleanup and state, with one subagent per item; a monolithic context is only reported, not fixed. Phase 3 loads argent-react-native-profiler to profile the key user flows, cross-references what it finds with the sweeps and fixes the biggest issues first: mechanical fixes in batches, architectural ones one per cycle. Only the main agent touches the device. Phase 4 visits every screen in scope and checks the console log for errors the fixes introduced, then lint runs once more. A measured interaction is first recorded as a replayable e2e test, with argent-create-e2e.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/software-mansion/argent/tree/b965c94827d6167fd2912a7ca5ad5505040ae4e0/packages/skills/skills/argent-react-native-optimization"
        },
        "tags": [
