      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Generates logos, brand identity mockups and SVG icons with Gemini, and designs slides, banners and social media images.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you need brand assets made: a logo, business cards and stationery, icons, a pitch deck, banners or social media images"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "searches bundled style, color and industry data to write a brief, then runs Python scripts that generate the images with Gemini"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "logo images, identity mockups in an HTML presentation, SVG icons, HTML slides, and banners and social images exported as PNG"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "a Gemini API key and two Python packages; social images also need headless Chrome, Playwright or Puppeteer"
            },
            {
              "label": "Hands off",
              "text": "brand voice, design tokens and shadcn or Tailwind work to its sibling skills brand, design-system and ui-styling"
            }
          ],
          "text": "An all-in-one design skill, written by ClaudeKit, that ships next to ui-ux-pro-max in the UI UX Pro Max repo. Logos start from a design brief that a BM25 search builds from 55 styles, 30 palettes and 25 industry guides; a script then generates them with Gemini, or with Atlas Cloud or MuAPI, always on a white background, and the agent offers an HTML preview gallery. A corporate identity program works the same way: pick deliverables such as business cards and letterheads, generate mockups with Gemini, ideally from your logo, and render them into an HTML presentation. Icons come out as SVG text from Gemini 3.1 Pro, in 15 styles, singly, in batches or at several sizes. Slides, banners and social images are built in HTML and CSS: banners at exact platform sizes with safe zones and one call to action; social images per platform, screenshotted at exact pixels, inspected and re-exported, with a report saved to plans/reports/. Brand voice, tokens and component styling go to the sibling skills brand, design-system and ui-styling, and banners and social images take style guidance from ui-ux-pro-max. When a script fails, the agent is told to fix it itself.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/nextlevelbuilder/ui-ux-pro-max-skill/tree/b7d5353e0130feb8c5574ef1251f8a1db1873ccb/cli/assets/skills/design"
