            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "an updated guidelines file and token files, a summary of the theme and colors, and checks on asset files and image colors"
            },
            {
              "label": "Stops",
              "text": "when your project already has a token source, such as :root variables or a Tailwind theme, rather than build a second one"
            }
          ],
          "text": "One of the design skills, written by ClaudeKit, that ship next to ui-ux-pro-max in the UI UX Pro Max repo. It treats docs/brand-guidelines.md as the brand's source of truth, with a starter template for new brands, and a script syncs it to design-tokens.json and design-tokens.css. Its update command asks for a theme name, primary, secondary and accent colors with hex codes, and mood keywords for image generation, or takes one of five presets such as ocean-professional; it then edits the guidelines, runs the sync, checks the output and reports the theme and the files it changed. The sync refuses to run beside an existing token system unless you pass --force for its own earlier output. Other scripts extract brand context to inject into prompts, validate an asset's name, size and format, and pull colors from an image to compare with the palette. References cover voice, visual identity, messaging, consistency, asset organization, color, typography, logo usage and approval checklists.",
