          "text": "One of the design skills, written by ClaudeKit, that ship next to ui-ux-pro-max in the UI UX Pro Max repo, and a fuller version of the banner section in its design skill. It starts by asking six questions: purpose, platform or size, copy, brand assets, style, and how many options, three by default. A bundled reference gives sizes, safe zones and 22 art styles, from minimalist and gradient to glassmorphism and neon. Each option is built in HTML and CSS with critical content in the central 70–80%, at most two typefaces, one call to action, text contrast of at least 4.5:1, and only the brand rules you supplied. Visuals come from your assets, CSS shapes and gradients, or an image generator if the agent has one, prompted without text so the copy stays editable. Each banner is captured as a PNG at its exact size and checked for dimensions, crop and fonts; then all options are shown together with their rationale, file path and size, and refined until you approve one. It handles banners only, not video, full websites or print production.",
