          "text": "A one-shot cheat sheet for Ponytail, a skill set that makes coding agents write the least code that fully solves a task. It shows the three levels: lite builds what was asked and names the smaller option, full is the default, and ultra also pushes back on the request before building. It lists the six skills, ponytail itself, ponytail-review, ponytail-audit, ponytail-debt, ponytail-gain and this card, and how to call them in Codex. It reminds you that \"stop ponytail\" or \"normal mode\" turns it off, explains how to hide the band Ponytail shows above the prompt in Claude Code or import past sessions into it, and how to set the default level with the PONYTAIL_DEFAULT_MODE variable or ~/.config/ponytail/config.json, including off. It also says how to turn on the plugin's auto-update in Claude Code. It's only useful once the other ponytail skills are installed.",
