              "text": "pulsing hotspots on features, narration timed to the screens, and callouts pulled from each screen's HTML text"
            }
          ],
          "text": "It finds your Stitch project and lists its screens, downloads each screenshot into assets/screens in walkthrough order, and records each screen's title, description, size and duration (3 to 5 seconds by default) in screens.json. It then reuses an existing Remotion project or creates one in video/, writes a slide component that zooms and fades each screen in, and a composition that sequences the slides with fade or slide transitions, titles, descriptions and a progress indicator. It opens Remotion Studio to preview and adjust timing, then renders the final file with the Remotion CLI or MCP server. It suggests three patterns: a simple slideshow, a feature highlight that zooms into parts of a screen, and a user flow with numbered steps. For deeper Remotion technique it points to Remotion's own skills.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/google-labs-code/stitch-skills/tree/0337446dadde6f8c94210444e2aa9d546126480f/plugins/stitch-build/skills/remotion"
