      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Generates YouTube thumbnails and Shorts or Instagram video covers through Higgsfield, from a truthful concept to targeted edits.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you need a thumbnail for a YouTube video, or a cover for a Short or an Instagram video"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "picks the strongest truthful \"information gap\" (a hook that makes viewers want to know more) from five or more concepts, then renders it in 4K through Higgsfield's CLI"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "image links with short labels such as \"shock / close-up\"; text-free by default, with a styled headline overlay or baked-in text on request"
            },
            {
              "label": "Keeps",
              "text": "up to three real people recognizable from your photos, plus your logo, kept flat or turned 3D"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "the higgsfield CLI, which it installs if missing, and a Higgsfield account; generations use credits"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike higgsfield-generate",
              "text": "that skill makes any image or video; this one follows thumbnail rules: one focal subject, readable at 120 pixels wide, no invented claims"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Higgsfield is a platform hosting many AI image, video and audio models. The agent asks only for what the brief leaves out: the video's topic and the promise the thumbnail may make, who appears (zero to three people; it never picks a stand-in face without asking), an optional style reference, logo or 2 to 4 word headline, and the ratio: 16:9 for YouTube, 9:16 for Shorts or 4:5 for Instagram. A reference thumbnail is analyzed for framing, palette and emotion but never sent to Higgsfield or copied. Prompts follow a fixed order, from frame and scene to an identity lock for each face, a lighting rig and the color grade. It offers about four variants when alternatives would help, capped at 16 generations, and checks each result, when the agent can see images, for matching faces, stray text and legibility at small size, retrying a failure at most twice. You pick one; it can then change only the expression, the background or the rim light with Seedream edits, leaving everything else untouched.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/higgsfield-ai/skills/tree/27000402070db19d958789d05b3b52b6f4718d7c/higgsfield-youtube-thumbnail"
        },
