      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Creates Mermaid diagrams and design documents from descriptions or source code, validating each diagram before adding it to your docs.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you need a flowchart, sequence, class, ER, state, C4 or architecture diagram, or a design document, from a description or your code"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "loads only the guide for that diagram type, writes the Mermaid code, saves it as a .mmd file and renders it to validate it before adding it to Markdown"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": ".mmd and PNG or SVG files in ./diagrams with image links in your Markdown; full design documents go in docs/design/"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "mermaid-cli (mmdc) and Python to validate and export images; writing diagram code alone needs neither"
            },
            {
              "label": "Style",
              "text": "Unicode symbols on nodes, such as 🔐 for auth and 💾 for databases, and high-contrast colors in every style"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike archify",
              "text": "which redraws diagrams as interactive HTML in its own style, it produces plain Mermaid that GitHub renders, plus images for Confluence"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A decision tree routes each request to one of its guides: activity diagrams for workflows, deployment diagrams for cloud and Kubernetes, architecture, sequence, or a GitHub wiki guide for class, ER and state diagrams. For existing code it has worked examples for Spring Boot, FastAPI, React, Python ETL, Express and Java web apps, such as deriving a deployment diagram from application.yml. Five templates cover architecture, API, feature, database and system design documents. Its rule is never to add a diagram to Markdown until it passes validation: a bundled script saves the .mmd, renders it with mermaid-cli and reports errors; on failure the agent checks a troubleshooting guide of 28 known errors, then searches the web. For GitHub, a fenced mermaid block is enough; for Confluence, Notion, Word or PDF it also exports PNG or SVG. Other scripts extract every diagram from a Markdown file, validate them, swap them for image links, or batch-convert a folder. PlantUML is left for the types Mermaid lacks, such as wireframes, use-case and timing diagrams.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/spillwavesolutions/design-doc-mermaid/tree/c36d83503d2ba9c1e51638dc2d8a34758a377dea"
        },
        "tags": [
