      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Publishes Markdown, HTML or plain-text articles and image posts to a WeChat Official Account, through its API or Chrome.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "an article or image post is ready and you want it in your WeChat Official Account (公众号) without pasting it in by hand"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "renders Markdown or plain text as themed WeChat HTML, uploads its images and cover, and sends it through WeChat's API or a logged-in Chrome"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "through the API, a draft in your account's drafts box, ready to review and publish from WeChat's dashboard"
            },
            {
              "label": "Also posts",
              "text": "image posts (贴图) of up to 9 pictures, through Chrome"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Bun or npx, and a WeChat Official Account with API credentials, or Chrome logged in to it"
            },
            {
              "label": "Keeps",
              "text": "your theme, color, author, comment settings and accounts in a preferences file it sets up on first run"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A publishing tool for WeChat Official Accounts that runs its own scripts. It takes an HTML file, a Markdown file or plain text; plain text is first saved as a dated Markdown file. Markdown gets one of four themes (default, grace, simple, modern) and a color, and ordinary external links become citations at the bottom unless you ask for inline links. It asks for a missing title or summary, or generates one from the content. API posts need a cover, which it takes from the command, the frontmatter, imgs/cover.png or the first image, stopping to ask when there is none. There are three ways in: the API, fast but only from an IP on the account's allowlist; a logged-in Chrome, which is slower and needs a QR-code login the first time; or the API through an SSH tunnel to a server whose IP is allowed, with the app secret staying on your machine. Several accounts can be set up and picked per post. On first use, before anything else, it asks setup questions and saves your preferences. Unlike baoyu-markdown-to-html, from the same repo, which only converts, this one also sends the result to your account.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/jimliu/baoyu-skills/tree/ca703c2d7c2c4399a1dc0cf82224f8551e05a96d/skills/baoyu-post-to-wechat"
        },
