          "text": "Its 21 layouts set the structure, such as a timeline, funnel, iceberg, Venn diagram or the default bento grid of topics; its 22 styles set the look, such as the default hand-made paper craft, claymation, chalkboard, blueprint, pixel art or LEGO bricks. Any layout works with any style, and asking for 信息图 or 高密度信息大图 (a dense information poster) puts a matching layout first among its suggestions. The agent saves your source, writes an analysis of its topic, data, tone and audience, then restructures it into sections with labels and visual elements. It always asks you to confirm the combination, the aspect ratio and, when the source is in another language, the language, unless you tell it to skip that. The full prompt is saved to a file before generating, so the image can be reproduced or made with another backend; with no backend available, it tells you and asks rather than drawing the image in SVG or HTML. If text in the image comes out wrong, it regenerates from a corrected prompt instead of patching the picture with code, keeping the flawed version for comparison. Defaults such as a preferred layout, style or backend are set on first run.",
