      },
      "skillMd": {
        "version": "ca703c2d7c2c4399a1dc0cf82224f8551e05a96d",
        "updated": "2026-11-06",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Generates a cover image for an article, combining a type, palette, rendering style, font, title text and mood.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "an article or post needs a cover image"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "reads the article, recommends a type, palette, rendering, font, amount of text and mood, and generates the cover once you confirm"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "cover.png, at 16:9 by default or 2.35:1, 4:3, 3:2, 1:1 or 3:4, with its prompt saved beside it"
            },
            {
              "label": "Choices",
              "text": "6 types, such as hero, metaphor or typography; 11 palettes; 7 renderings, such as flat vector, hand-drawn, pixel or chalk"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "an image generator: your agent's own (as in Codex or Cursor), baoyu-image-gen with an API key, or a logged-in codex CLI"
            }
          ],
          "text": "On first run it asks setup questions and saves preferences such as a watermark, default aspect and output folder; --quick skips that setup and the confirmation, though it still asks for the aspect ratio unless you give one. Otherwise it asks about the dimensions in one round of questions, with its recommendation listed first. Reference images you give it can guide the style, palette or composition. The title is taken exactly from you or the source, never invented, figures are simplified silhouettes rather than realistic people, and 40 to 60 percent of the image is left as breathing room. If the title comes out misspelled in the image, it regenerates from a corrected prompt instead of patching the picture. Covers go in their own cover-image folder by default, or next to the article.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/jimliu/baoyu-skills/tree/ca703c2d7c2c4399a1dc0cf82224f8551e05a96d/skills/baoyu-cover-image"
        },
