        "updated": "2026-11-06",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Turns an article or notes into a deck of AI-generated slide images, merged into PPTX and PDF.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you want a deck from an article or notes, mostly to read and share rather than to present live"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "suggests a style, audience and slide count, writes an outline and one prompt per slide, generates every slide as an image, then merges them"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "slide PNGs, plus a PPTX and a PDF made of those images, with the outline and prompts, in one folder"
            },
            {
              "label": "Styles",
              "text": "17 presets, such as blueprint (the default), chalkboard, corporate, notion, scientific or pixel art, or your own mix of texture, mood, typography and density"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Bun or npx to merge, and an image generator: your agent's own (as in Codex or Cursor), baoyu-image-gen with an API key, or a logged-in codex CLI"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Decks are designed to be read without a speaker: slides explain themselves and flow when scrolled, which shapes their density and layout. The agent analyzes the source, suggests a preset from its keywords and a slide count from its length, from 5 to 10 slides under 1,000 words to 20 to 30 beyond 5,000, then asks five questions at once: style, audience, count, and whether you want to review the outline and the prompts before any image is made. You can stop after the outline or the prompts, start from existing prompts, or regenerate single slides, editing a slide's prompt first. Slides render in batches of four by default, and reference images can set the style, palette or layout of every slide. If a slide's text comes out wrong, it regenerates instead of patching the image. If the deck's folder already exists, it asks whether to regenerate, back up first or stop.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/jimliu/baoyu-skills/tree/ca703c2d7c2c4399a1dc0cf82224f8551e05a96d/skills/baoyu-slide-deck"
        },
