        "updated": "2026-11-06",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Turns a topic or source text into an educational comic, from storyboard and characters to finished pages and a PDF.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you want a topic, a biography or a tutorial told as an educational comic, such as a Logicomix-style story"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "analyzes the material, asks for art style, tone and layout, writes a storyboard and character sheet, then generates each page"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "comic pages as PNGs and a merged PDF, with the storyboard, character definitions and prompts, in one folder"
            },
            {
              "label": "Looks",
              "text": "6 art styles, such as ligne claire, manga or ink brush; 7 tones; and layouts from standard panels to cinematic, webtoon and four-panel"
            },
            {
              "label": "Stays consistent",
              "text": "recurring characters, by generating a character reference sheet first and passing it along with every page"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Bun or npx to merge the PDF, and an image generator: your agent's own (as in Codex or Cursor), baoyu-image-gen with an API key, or a logged-in codex CLI"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Five presets add their own rules: ohmsha (manga that explains through visual metaphors and gadgets rather than talking heads), wuxia (ink brush and martial-arts action), shoujo (romantic manga), concept-story (a system of visual symbols and a growth arc) and four-panel (minimalist strips with a setup, development, twist and conclusion). Confirming the style is required; reviewing the storyboard and the prompts before images are made is optional. You can stop after the storyboard or the prompts, generate from existing prompts, or redo single pages, editing a page's prompt first. Once the character sheet exists, pages render in batches of four by default. Questions, storyboard, prompts and summaries all use your language or the one you set. Sensitive public figures are drawn stylized, and wrong text on a page means regenerating it, not patching the image. Preferences such as a watermark and a default art style are set up on first run.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/jimliu/baoyu-skills/tree/ca703c2d7c2c4399a1dc0cf82224f8551e05a96d/skills/baoyu-comic"
