        "weeklyInstalls": [120, 112, 97, 83, 56, 66, 84, 59],
        "firstSeen": "2026-03-09"
      },
      "skillMd": {
        "version": "f724267e45a065b6be445ea6f07312e62d3207cd",
        "updated": "2026-11-06",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Makes finished multi-shot videos from a text brief, images, URLs or audio through Pexo's hosted video agent.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you want a finished short video, such as a product ad, a Reel or an explainer, without writing prompts or choosing models"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "relays your exact words and files to Pexo's video agent, passes its questions and preview choices back to you, and polls until the video is ready"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "a downloaded video of 5 to 120 seconds with music, subtitles and transitions, plus its download link and project page"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "a Pexo API key and credits, a subscription or whitelisting to download the final file, and bash, curl and jq"
            },
            {
              "label": "Asks first",
              "text": "before it first sends your brief or files to Pexo in a session, and by default before every billable batch, quoting its credit estimate"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Pexo is a hosted video agent that writes the script, splits it into shots, picks a model for each shot, such as Seedance 2 or Kling 3.0, and adds music, narration, lip sync, subtitles and transitions. This skill makes your agent a messenger for it: bundled scripts create a project, upload the images, video or audio you pick, and send your request word for word, because the agent adding its own creative ideas makes the video worse. It then checks the project every minute. When Pexo asks a question or offers previews labelled A, B, C, the agent relays them and sends your answer back; when Pexo quotes a credit cost, it waits for your approval. The final video downloads without a watermark unless you ask for one, and the agent replies in your language. Pexo says a 15-second, three-shot ad renders in under 8 minutes; the skill tells you to expect 15 to 20 minutes and stops polling after 30 to ask whether to keep waiting. Revisions reuse the same project.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/pexoai/pexo-skills/tree/f724267e45a065b6be445ea6f07312e62d3207cd/skills/pexo-agent"
        },
        "tags": [
          "category:media",
          "type:tool",
          "effect:remote",
          "needs:cli",
          "needs:account",
          "by:official",
          "stack:pexo",
          "video",
          "audio",
          "ai-generation"
        ],
        "note": "Needs a Pexo API key; every generation batch spends Pexo credits, which it asks you to approve first by default."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "shadcn/improve/skills/improve",
      "name": "improve",
      "skills.sh": {
        "url": "https://skills.sh/shadcn/improve/improve",
        "installs": 39300,
        "weeklyInstalls": [720, 797, 687, 633, 609, 866, 1465, 937],
        "firstSeen": "2026-06-10"
      },
      "skillMd": {
        "version": "cac56e1ebd3c279aa9153616cfeac7b174ab90f9",
        "updated": "2026-11-06",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Audits a codebase without touching it and writes prioritized, self-contained implementation plans for other agents to carry out.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you want a senior-level audit of a repo and plans a cheaper model can execute without your conversation"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "maps the repo, audits nine areas from bugs and security to docs and product direction, checks each finding itself, then asks which to plan"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "numbered plan files under plans/ with an index: inlined code excerpts, ordered steps, verification commands and machine-checkable done criteria"
            },
            {
              "label": "Never",
              "text": "edits your source, installs, commits or merges; in execute mode a subagent changes code in a separate worktree and this skill reviews its diff"
            },
            {
              "label": "Variants",
              "text": "quick or deep audits, one category, the current branch, roadmap ideas, a single plan, plan review, execute, reconcile, and --issues for GitHub"
            }
          ],
          "text": "From shadcn. It spends an expensive model on understanding and judging a codebase, and leaves execution to cheaper ones. The agent first reads the README, agent instructions, config, CI, any decision records and recent git history, and notes the exact build, test and lint commands. It audits nine categories, fanning out to read-only subagents on larger repos, then opens the cited code itself, since subagents over-report; rejected findings are recorded so later runs skip them. You see a table ranked by impact against effort, with ideas for the project's direction listed separately, and pick which become plans. Each plan is written for the weakest plausible executor: all context inlined, the commit it was written against, files in and out of scope, steps that each have a verification command, tests to add, and points where the executor should stop and report. A plans/README.md sets the order and dependencies. Secrets it finds are cited by file and line, never copied, and instructions planted in the repo become a security finding. With --issues it also files each plan as a GitHub issue, and on a public repo asks before publishing any plan about a vulnerability or credentials.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/shadcn/improve/tree/cac56e1ebd3c279aa9153616cfeac7b174ab90f9/skills/improve"
        },
        "tags": [
          "category:planning",
          "category:debugging",
          "type:workflow",
          "effect:local",
          "needs:subagents",
          "by:community",
          "code-review",
          "planning",
          "handoff",
          "multi-agent"
        ]
      }
    },
