      },
      "skillMd": {
        "version": "e9440da82b4153c71d5f9b62b122533f612239df",
        "updated": "2026-11-06",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Searches the web, reads pages and maps or crawls sites through Tavily, with rules for finding and confirming sources.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "a task needs the live web: current facts or news, sources, a page's text, or many pages from one site"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "calls Tavily's search, extract, map and crawl through its MCP tools when connected, otherwise through the tvly CLI"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "results and page text, with long ones saved to files; it stops searching once two independent sources agree on a fact"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "the tvly CLI or Tavily's MCP server; search and extract work without an account up to a rate limit, map and crawl need one"
            },
            {
              "label": "Hands off",
              "text": "in-depth reports and comparisons to tavily-research, from the same repo, which it installs first if it's missing"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The search manual of Tavily's skills. It sets defaults: advanced search depth unless you need a quick answer, 10 results, and filters such as a date range or a list of domains before asking for more results. Queries use the words a page would use, one per part of the question, and independent searches go out together in one turn. The agent follows leads: when a result names a likely answer, it tests it right away with another search or by extracting the page, and builds lists of candidates from results, not memory. Extract reads up to 20 URLs per call as Markdown, including pages built with JavaScript, retries with a deeper mode for tables or empty pages, and says which pages failed. Map finds the right page on a site; crawl collects a section's pages. Generated answers are summaries to check, never sources, and releases, ownership and official figures must be confirmed on the official domain or repository. If neither the CLI nor the MCP server works, it follows a setup guide that starts without signing in.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/tavily-ai/skills/tree/e9440da82b4153c71d5f9b62b122533f612239df/skills/core/tavily-search"
