            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "the mmx-cli npm package and a MiniMax API key or login"
            },
            {
              "label": "Defaults",
              "text": "MiniMax-M3.1-Flash for text, which needs a MiniMax plan; image-01 for images, Hailuo 2.3 for video, speech-2.8-hd for speech"
            }
          ],
          "text": "MiniMax's own guide to its command line. It lists each command with its flags: text chat with system prompts, tool definitions and multi-turn messages; image generation with aspect ratio, count, seed and a subject reference; video from a prompt or from first and last frames, which either waits for the file or returns a task ID; speech synthesis with voice, speed, pitch and optional .srt subtitles; transcription of audio up to 50 MB and 500 seconds into text, JSON with word timestamps, SRT or VTT; image description; web search; and a quota check. In agent contexts it uses flags such as --non-interactive, --quiet and --output json, so stdout is clean data to pipe, and exit codes tell auth, quota, timeout and content-filter failures apart. It can export every command as a JSON tool schema for agent frameworks and set a default model per modality. For MiniMax's H3 video model it points to a separate skill.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/minimax-ai/cli/tree/38aba5f26173dd1065b115b221d79c9ddd87c6bb/skill"
        },
