      "skillMd": {
        "version": "4bde3168b43c0655c4d00ea2726e631719908a6d",
        "updated": "2026-11-06",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Guides schema and data migrations in Sequelize, TypeORM and Prisma, with zero-downtime column changes and rollback strategies.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you're changing a database schema, transforming existing data or moving between databases, and want a way back if it fails"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "gives the agent migration patterns with up and down steps, mostly in Sequelize, plus the TypeORM and Prisma basics"
            },
            {
              "label": "Zero downtime",
              "text": "a column rename runs in steps: add the new column and copy the data, switch the app, then drop the old column"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "migrations written along those patterns; it adds no steps or files of its own"
            }
          ],
          "text": "It's a reference, not a workflow. It opens with a create-table migration in each of Sequelize, TypeORM and Prisma, with the commands to run them. The rest is Sequelize code: adding a column with a default; renaming a column without downtime by adding the new one, copying the data, updating the app and only then removing the old one; and changing a column's type on a large table by adding a new column, casting the data into it, dropping the old one and renaming the new one. A data migration splits an address string into street, city and state, with a down step that rebuilds it. For rollbacks, it wraps changes in a transaction, or copies the table to a backup first, checks the result and restores the backup if the check fails. A separate file adds a five-phase blue-green migration (add the column, write to both, backfill, read from the new one, remove the old) and a migration that picks MySQL's JSON or PostgreSQL's JSONB column type depending on the database.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/wshobson/agents/tree/4bde3168b43c0655c4d00ea2726e631719908a6d/plugins/framework-migration/skills/database-migration"
        },
