      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Builds design systems from layered design tokens, light, dark and multi-brand theming, and consistent component APIs.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you're creating design tokens, adding theme switching or multi-brand themes, or building a component library"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "organizes tokens in three layers: primitives (raw values), semantic tokens (what a value means, such as text-primary) and component tokens (button-bg)"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "tokens as CSS custom properties, a theme switcher that follows the system setting, and components with variant and size systems"
            },
            {
              "label": "Also covers",
              "text": "a Style Dictionary config that builds CSS, SCSS, iOS and Android files from JSON token files"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A reference for the foundations of a design system. Tokens are named by purpose rather than look (text-primary, not dark-gray): semantic tokens refer to primitives, and component tokens to semantic ones. Its code, mostly in a separate file, shows the three token layers as CSS custom properties, a React theme provider that switches between light, dark and the system's color-scheme setting and remembers the choice, a button with variants and sizes built with class-variance-authority, and the Style Dictionary config. It also lists, without examples, compound, polymorphic, slot-based and headless components, reduced-motion and high-contrast modes, and syncing tokens from Figma in CI. Its rules: document how each token is used, version tokens like an API with semver, test every theme with every component, automate the token pipeline and retire tokens gradually. Common problems it names are token sprawl, mixed naming conventions, tokens that ignore dark mode, hardcoded values, tokens that reference each other in loops, and tokens missing on some platforms.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/wshobson/agents/tree/4bde3168b43c0655c4d00ea2726e631719908a6d/plugins/ui-design/skills/design-system-patterns"
