      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Sets up and runs JavaScript monorepos with pnpm workspaces and Turborepo or Nx: shared packages and configs, build caching, CI and publishing.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you're starting a monorepo, merging several repos into one, or speeding up its builds and tests"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "recommends pnpm workspaces and Turborepo for most teams, calls Nx feature-rich but complex, and shows how to set them up"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "apps and shared packages, a turbo.json task pipeline with caching, shared TypeScript and ESLint configs, and releases with Changesets"
            },
            {
              "label": "Watch for",
              "text": "circular and phantom dependencies, wrong cache inputs, and Turborepo 2 rejecting a config that still uses the old pipeline key"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Monorepo practice for JavaScript and TypeScript. It weighs the gains (shared code, atomic commits across projects, consistent tooling, easier refactoring) against the costs (build times at scale, CI complexity, access control, a large Git repository), ranks the tools (pnpm over npm or Yarn workspaces; Turborepo for most, Nx feature-rich but complex, Lerna in maintenance mode) and walks through a Turborepo setup with apps and shared packages. Its rules: keep dependency versions consistent, centralize ESLint, TypeScript and Prettier configs, keep the dependency graph acyclic, set cache inputs and outputs correctly, share types between frontend and backend, unit-test packages and test apps end to end, and version with Changesets, published from a GitHub Actions workflow. A separate file covers pnpm workspace commands, Nx setup and tasks for affected projects, shared configs, patterns for sharing UI, utilities and types, local and remote caching, and CI that deploys only the apps that changed.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/wshobson/agents/tree/4bde3168b43c0655c4d00ea2726e631719908a6d/plugins/developer-essentials/skills/monorepo-management"
