        "updated": "2026-11-06",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Translates a file, a URL or pasted text in one of three modes, from a single quick pass to a reviewed, polished translation.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you want an article or document translated so it reads as if written in the target language, Simplified Chinese by default"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "analyzes the source, builds a translation prompt with a glossary, translates, and in refined mode critiques, revises and polishes"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "translation.md in a folder next to the source, with each intermediate step's file kept beside it"
            },
            {
              "label": "Modes",
              "text": "quick translates in one pass; normal, the default, analyzes first; refined adds a critique, a revision and a final polish"
            },
            {
              "label": "Long texts",
              "text": "from 4,000 words, its script splits the text at Markdown blocks and subagents draft the chunks in parallel, when the agent has them"
            },
            {
              "label": "Keeps",
              "text": "the Markdown formatting, facts and data, and consistent terms from your glossaries plus a built-in English-to-Chinese one"
            },
            {
              "label": "Asks first",
              "text": "target language, mode, audience, style and where to save preferences, before its first translation"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Bun or npx, to split long texts"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Its rule is to rewrite rather than translate word for word: natural word order, long sentences broken up, idioms rendered by meaning, specialized terms followed by the original in parentheses the first time, and a few bold explanations where the audience may lack context. Audience presets (general, technical, academic, business) set how much it explains; style presets such as storytelling (the default), formal, literal, humorous or elegant set the voice, and both accept your own description. Saying 快翻 or quick picks quick mode, 精翻 or refined the refined one. After a normal translation you can reply 继续润色 or refine to run the review steps on it. Source frontmatter is kept, with its fields renamed with a source prefix and translated values added. At the end it lists images that probably still carry text in the source language, and leaves them alone unless you ask. Glossaries can be set inline or as files in its preferences, or passed per run.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/jimliu/baoyu-skills/tree/ca703c2d7c2c4399a1dc0cf82224f8551e05a96d/skills/baoyu-translate"
        },
        "tags": [
          "category:writing",
          "type:workflow",
          "effect:local",
          "needs:cli",
          "by:community",
          "writing"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "jimliu/baoyu-skills/.claude/skills/release-skills",
      "name": "release-skills",
      "skills.sh": {
        "url": "https://skills.sh/jimliu/baoyu-skills/release-skills",
        "installs": 25900,
        "weeklyInstalls": [272, 260, 196, 257, 135, 125, 142, 140],
        "firstSeen": "2026-01-19"
      },
      "skillMd": {
        "version": "ca703c2d7c2c4399a1dc0cf82224f8551e05a96d",
        "updated": "2026-11-06",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Releases a project: bumps the version from its commits, writes changelogs in each language, commits, tags and publishes a GitHub Release.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "a Node.js, Python, Rust, Claude plugin or plain VERSION-file project is ready for a new version"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "reads the commits since the last tag, picks a semantic version bump, updates the version file and changelogs, commits and creates an annotated tag"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "updated changelogs in every language your repo keeps, such as CHANGELOG.zh.md, a release commit, a tag and, if you agree, a GitHub Release"
            },
            {
              "label": "When it asks",
              "text": "just before the release commit, for the version, pushing and the GitHub Release; by then it has already committed pending changes per module and written the changelogs"
            },
            {
              "label": "Watch out",
              "text": "it triggers on \"push\" too, and runs all its release steps even when you only ask to push uncommitted changes"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "git, and the gh CLI signed in for GitHub Releases"
            },
            {
              "label": "Origin",
              "text": "the release tool baoyu-skills uses on itself, kept in its .claude folder rather than among its published skills"
            }
          ],
          "text": "It detects the version file (package.json, pyproject.toml, Cargo.toml, marketplace.json or VERSION) and every CHANGELOG, HISTORY or CHANGES file, telling each one's language from its filename suffix. A breaking change means a major bump, a feat commit a minor one and anything else a patch, unless you force one with a flag. Each changelog gets entries written in its own language rather than translated, with (by @username) after changes merged from anyone but the repo owner. Changes are grouped by skill or module, as in a repo of skills/<name> folders, committed separately with conventional commit messages, and the READMEs checked for options or examples that need updating. A dry run previews everything without changing anything, and a backfill mode creates missing GitHub Releases for existing tags from their changelog sections, without bumping versions. A .releaserc.yml can override the detected files, changelog sections and tag format, or hand packaging and publishing to your own hooks.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/jimliu/baoyu-skills/tree/ca703c2d7c2c4399a1dc0cf82224f8551e05a96d/.claude/skills/release-skills"
        },
        "tags": [
          "category:engineering",
          "type:workflow",
          "effect:remote",
          "needs:cli",
          "by:community",
          "stack:git",
          "stack:github",
          "git"
        ],
        "note": "It also triggers on \"push\", and then runs its whole release process even when you only meant to push."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "jimliu/baoyu-skills/skills/baoyu-youtube-transcript",
      "name": "baoyu-youtube-transcript",
      "skills.sh": {
        "url": "https://skills.sh/jimliu/baoyu-skills/baoyu-youtube-transcript",
        "installs": 22300,
        "weeklyInstalls": [371, 355, 193, 182, 243, 272, 297, 326],
        "firstSeen": "2026-03-22"
      },
      "skillMd": {
        "version": "ca703c2d7c2c4399a1dc0cf82224f8551e05a96d",
        "updated": "2026-11-06",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Downloads a YouTube video's transcript as Markdown or SRT, with chapters, speaker labels and its cover image, without an API key.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you want the words of a YouTube video, or its thumbnail, saved as a file"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "fetches captions with its bundled script through YouTube's InnerTube API, falling back to yt-dlp when YouTube blocks it"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "transcript.md with timestamped paragraphs, or transcript.srt, plus meta.json and imgs/cover.jpg, under youtube-transcript/<channel>/<title>/"
            },
            {
              "label": "Speakers",
              "text": "by default a subagent labels who is speaking, from the title, channel, description and conversation cues, and splits the text into chapters"
            },
            {
              "label": "Languages",
              "text": "lists the available transcripts when you name no language, takes a language order, and can translate"
            },
            {
              "label": "Caches",
              "text": "raw data per video, so reformatting it or asking only for the cover doesn't fetch it again"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Bun or npx, plus yt-dlp as a fallback, which the agent sets up itself if it's missing; no API key or browser"
            }
          ],
          "text": "It works with manual and auto-generated captions and takes watch, youtu.be, embed and shorts links or bare video IDs, several at once. Chapters come from the timestamps in the video's description; without them, the text is grouped into paragraphs. For speaker identification, which it uses by default, the script saves a raw file with the metadata and the transcript in SRT form, then a subagent, which can be a cheaper model, rewrites it with speaker labels, short paragraphs and timestamps. Sentences are split on punctuation, including Chinese, Japanese and Korean, with timestamps shared out by length. When YouTube flags it as a bot, the script retries other client identities, then yt-dlp; passing your browser's cookies to yt-dlp is the last resort. It can skip auto-generated or manual transcripts, and --refresh ignores the cache.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/jimliu/baoyu-skills/tree/ca703c2d7c2c4399a1dc0cf82224f8551e05a96d/skills/baoyu-youtube-transcript"
        },
        "tags": [
          "category:browser",
          "type:tool",
          "effect:local",
          "needs:cli",
          "needs:subagents",
          "by:community",
          "stack:youtube",
          "video",
          "scraping"
        ],
        "note": "When YouTube blocks its requests, it falls back to yt-dlp, and the agent installs yt-dlp without asking if it's missing."
      }
    },
