      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Runs a scenario step by step through Playwright MCP, then writes a Playwright TypeScript test from it and runs it until it passes.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you have a scenario to test in a web app and want a Playwright test written for it"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "carries out the scenario's steps one by one in the browser with the Playwright MCP tools before writing any test code"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "a TypeScript test using @playwright/test, saved in the tests directory, run and reworked until it passes"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "the Playwright MCP server connected, and Playwright in the project to run the test"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike playwright-explore-website",
              "text": "which explores a site to find what's worth testing, this turns one scenario you give into a passing test"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Test code written from a scenario's description alone is a guess about the page. This skill forbids that: the agent may not generate test code prematurely or from the scenario alone. It first performs every step of the scenario itself, one at a time, with the tools of the Playwright MCP server. Only once all steps are done does it write a Playwright test in TypeScript with @playwright/test, based on the session's history of those steps. It saves the file in the tests directory, runs it, and keeps iterating until the test passes. If you don't give a scenario, it asks for one first.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/github/awesome-copilot/tree/797337f33f73e35d08d82f840e21c4b8c4932d88/skills/playwright-generate-test"
