      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Writes a specification file for the purpose you give, with numbered requirements, interfaces, acceptance criteria and a test strategy, worded for AI agents.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you want requirements, constraints and interfaces written down in a form another agent can follow without guessing"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "fills a fixed template: purpose and scope, definitions, requirements, interfaces, acceptance criteria, test strategy, rationale, dependencies, examples, validation criteria and related specs"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "one Markdown file with front matter in /spec/, named spec-<purpose>-<name>.md, the purpose being schema, tool, data, infrastructure, process, architecture or design"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike create-implementation-plan",
              "text": "from the same repo, which lays out the phased tasks to build something, this defines what it must do"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A spec template meant for AI readers: precise, explicit language, no idioms or metaphors, every acronym defined, and a document that stands on its own. Each requirement gets a prefixed ID, REQ-001 for requirements, SEC- for security, CON- for constraints, GUD- for guidelines and PAT- for patterns to follow, and acceptance criteria use Given-When-Then where it fits. Dependencies are written as what is needed, such as \"an OAuth 2.0 authentication library\", rather than a package and version. The template's test section suggests MSTest, FluentAssertions and Moq for .NET apps and GitHub Actions for CI, so expect to swap those for your stack. It has no interview step: it writes from the purpose you give it.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/github/awesome-copilot/tree/797337f33f73e35d08d82f840e21c4b8c4932d88/skills/create-specification"
        },
