          ],
          "text": "Reference material and short build steps for web game development. Its core is the game loop: read input, update state, render, driven by requestAnimationFrame. Around it, the skill covers when to use Canvas 2D, WebGL, SVG or CSS; AABB, circle and SAT collision in 2D, bounding volumes and raycasting in 3D; simple Newtonian movement and gravity; and the Web Audio API. Short workflows outline a basic 2D game, a 3D game built on a framework, and publishing: optimizing assets, testing across browsers, choosing a platform, monetizing and promoting. Starter templates in its assets folder include a Breakout-style paddle game, a maze game with device-orientation controls, a Phaser platformer and a simple 2D engine with collisions. References cover web APIs, algorithms, 3D and WebXR, controls, publishing and a glossary. A troubleshooting table answers common problems: a blank canvas, game speed that varies with frame rate, unreliable collisions, audio that won't play before a click, and a lost WebGL context.",
