              "text": "it holds the exact commands and conventions agents need, not general project information for people"
            }
          ],
          "text": "AGENTS.md is an open format, documented at agents.md, for a \"README for agents\": one Markdown file at the repo root that coding tools such as Cursor, Aider and Gemini CLI read for project context. The skill explains the format, then has the agent analyze the project's languages, frameworks, package managers, test frameworks and layout, and find its key workflows in package.json scripts, Makefiles, CI files and documentation. From those it writes the essential sections, project overview, setup commands, development workflow, testing instructions, code style, and build and deployment, plus optional ones on security, monorepo navigation, pull requests and debugging, starting from a template and a real example from agents.md. It wants exact commands in code blocks rather than vague descriptions, and has the agent check that each documented command works. In a monorepo, nested AGENTS.md files go in subprojects, and the one closest to a file takes precedence.",
