        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Applies prompt engineering techniques, such as few-shot examples, chain-of-thought, structured outputs and system prompt design, to prompts for production LLM applications.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you're writing, optimizing or debugging the prompts inside an LLM application, or a prompt gives inconsistent or unparseable output"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "covers few-shot example selection, chain-of-thought with self-verification, structured outputs with Pydantic, prompt templates, system prompts and recovery from malformed output"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "prompts built from those patterns, and metrics to track them by: accuracy, consistency, latency, token use and the share of valid outputs"
            },
            {
              "label": "Works with",
              "text": "Python, with examples that use the Anthropic SDK and LangChain"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A reference for prompts that run inside an application rather than in a chat. Its patterns: few-shot prompting with examples picked by semantic similarity, chain-of-thought with a verification step, structured outputs enforced by a Pydantic schema, progressive disclosure (start with a plain instruction and add constraints, reasoning, then examples only when needed), recovery when output fails to parse, and role-based system prompts. It also shows prompts combined with retrieval (RAG) and with validation, shorter prompts that save tokens, and caching a long system prompt. Best practices: be specific, show examples rather than describe, enforce schemas, test on varied inputs, and version prompts like code. Pitfalls include starting complex, examples that don't match the task, overflowing the context window and assuming output is always well-formed.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/wshobson/agents/tree/4bde3168b43c0655c4d00ea2726e631719908a6d/plugins/llm-application-dev/skills/prompt-engineering-patterns"
        },
