      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Builds layouts that adapt to any screen with mobile-first breakpoints, container queries, fluid typography and CSS Grid.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you're building a layout that has to work from phones to large desktops, or components that adapt to the space they're placed in"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "gives the agent patterns for container queries, fluid type with clamp(), Grid and Flexbox layouts, navigation, images, tables and mobile viewport units"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "layouts built mobile-first, with breakpoints set where the content needs them rather than per device; it adds no steps or files of its own"
            },
            {
              "label": "Works with",
              "text": "plain CSS, plus React components styled with Tailwind in about half the examples"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A reference of modern CSS techniques for responsive layouts. Container queries let a component respond to the width of its container rather than the viewport. Fluid typography and spacing scale between a minimum and a maximum with clamp(). It gives a mobile-first breakpoint scale from 640 to 1536 pixels, matching Tailwind's, and patterns for auto-fitting grids, a navigation that collapses behind a menu button on small screens, images with art direction through <picture>, tables that scroll sideways or turn into cards on mobile, and the dynamic viewport units that fix 100vh on mobile browsers. Best practices: start from mobile styles, set breakpoints by content, prefer fluid values to fixed ones, keep touch targets at least 44 by 44 pixels, use logical properties for internationalization, and test on real devices. Common issues it names include horizontal overflow, fixed pixel widths, squashed images and overlays that break across screen sizes.",
