            }
          ],
          "text": "A reference for pipeline architecture rather than one CI product. The SKILL.md says what to give it and what it produces, then troubleshoots five failures: a shallow /ping health check that hides an unreachable database, an Argo Rollouts canary stuck because its Prometheus query returns no data, a production approval gate with no reviewer assigned, a Dockerfile that copies the source before installing dependencies, and a rollback that leaves new migrations under old code (keep migrations additive, with undo scripts). Its first reference file covers the stages from build to rollback; manual, delayed, multi-approver and metric-based gates; a decision table for rolling, blue-green, canary, recreate and feature-flag releases; shallow and deep health endpoints; a post-deploy check script; automated and manual rollback with kubectl; and DORA metrics. A second file holds full pipelines for GitHub Actions, GitLab CI and Azure Pipelines, multi-region canaries, advanced Argo Rollouts, expand/contract migrations, deployment freeze windows and Slack notifications. It points to github-actions-templates, gitlab-ci-patterns and secrets-management for one platform's details or for secrets.",
