      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Guides automated changelogs and release notes from Conventional Commits, in Keep a Changelog format, with setups for tools like semantic-release and git-cliff.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you want changelogs and release notes generated from commit history instead of written by hand, or a team to agree on a commit message format"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "explains Conventional Commits, how each commit type maps to a Keep a Changelog section, and which version number a change bumps"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "commit message examples, a release notes template, and six automation setups in its reference file, from commitlint with husky to semantic-release and git-cliff"
            },
            {
              "label": "Rules",
              "text": "one logical change per commit, validate messages with commitlint and in CI, never hand-edit a generated changelog, always mark breaking changes"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A reference for automating release documentation. Conventional Commits is a commit message format, type(scope): description, where the type (feat, fix, perf and so on) decides which changelog section a change lands in and whether the major, minor or patch number goes up; a ! or a BREAKING CHANGE footer marks a breaking change. Keep a Changelog is a changelog layout with an Unreleased section and Added, Changed, Deprecated, Removed, Fixed and Security headings under each version. The SKILL.md itself holds commit message examples, the body of an internal release notes template (summary, highlights, breaking changes, upgrade guide, known issues, updated dependencies) and do's and don'ts. The commit type table, the version rules and most of the changelog example sit in its reference file, which also gives six ways to automate it: conventional-changelog tooling with commitlint and a husky commit hook, standard-version, semantic-release for fully automated releases, a GitHub Actions release workflow, git-cliff, and commitizen for Python projects, plus a GitHub release notes template.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/wshobson/agents/tree/4bde3168b43c0655c4d00ea2726e631719908a6d/plugins/documentation-generation/skills/changelog-automation"
        },
