            }
          ],
          "text": "A reference of visual design basics with ready-made values. Typography gets a nine-step scale from 12 to 48 pixels, line heights for headings, body text and labels, three safe font pairings, fluid sizes with clamp(), a reading width of 65 characters and font-display: swap to avoid layout shift. Spacing follows an 8-point grid, a scale from 4 to 64 pixels, with suggested gaps for cards, sections, form fields, buttons and icons, and a vertical rhythm for prose. Colors are semantic tokens, named by purpose (primary, success, error) rather than by appearance, with a gray scale, a dark theme that swaps the same variables, WCAG minimum contrast ratios and a TypeScript function that computes contrast. Icons get a five-size scale and a React SVG component. A quick start puts fonts, font sizes, a brand color and extra spacing into a Tailwind config. It closes with rules, such as two or three font weights per family and mobile-first design, and common issues such as magic numbers, missing hover, focus and disabled states, and no plan for dark mode.",
