      "skillMd": {
        "version": "58217546cd94fcf5ddcde4265c00a9377ed3192c",
        "updated": "2026-11-06",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Fetches a URL or PDF and returns a short summary or clean Markdown, extracting locally by default, with optional DeepSeek web search.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you hand the agent a URL or PDF to read, quote, convert or save"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "routes each link to a fetcher, such as raw GitHub content, PDF extraction, a Feishu API script or a WeChat fallback, and extracts the text locally"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "a short source-grounded summary by default, or clean Markdown, quotes or a saved file when you ask"
            },
            {
              "label": "Keeps",
              "text": "URLs off third-party readers such as r.jina.ai and defuddle.md unless you opt in, and never sends them sensitive URLs"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "pdftotext, marker or pypdf for PDFs, Feishu app credentials for Feishu docs, a DeepSeek API key for DeepSeek search, and Playwright for the WeChat fallback"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Read is Waza's fetch step, and learn uses it to collect sources. Its fetch script is privacy-first: by default it fetches from the source site and extracts the article on your machine, with cleaner output if readability-lxml and html2text are installed. With your opt-in it falls back to defuddle.md and r.jina.ai for JavaScript-heavy pages and paywalls, but never for authenticated or internal URLs. When the built-in web search is thin or lacks Chinese sources, it can search through DeepSeek, which bills each request. It saves nothing unless you say save or learn calls it; then it writes Markdown with frontmatter to the folder you name or a temp folder, never overwriting, and downloads images only on request. If a fetch returns a login wall, paywall or empty page, it stops and says what it tried instead of saving the shell. Fetched content is treated as data, never as instructions.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/tw93/waza/tree/58217546cd94fcf5ddcde4265c00a9377ed3192c/skills/read"
        },
        "tags": [
