        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Drives TV apps on Apple TV, Android TV and Fire TV through Argent: reads focus, navigates with the D-pad remote, types and takes screenshots.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "the agent needs to use or test an app on an Apple TV simulator, an Android TV emulator or Amazon Fire TV (Vega)"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "reads which element has focus, moves focus with one remote-button path ending in select, then checks focus again"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "an agent that navigates by focus as a remote does, never by tapping coordinates"
            },
            {
              "label": "E2E tests",
              "text": "only on Fire TV (Vega); on Apple TV and Android TV it reports that limitation"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "the Argent MCP server; for Fire TV, the vega CLI, which the agent runs to stop the virtual device and set up Fast Refresh"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike argent-device-interact",
              "text": "which drives touch screens with taps and gestures, this drives focus-based TV interfaces"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Part of Software Mansion's Argent toolkit, which lets the agent control simulators, emulators and devices. A TV is driven by focus, not touch, so this skill swaps taps and gestures for a loop: describe the screen to find the focused element and the target, send one remote-button path ending in select, such as down, right, select, counting rows and columns from the element frames, then describe again to confirm. On Fire TV's Vega the highlighted item is often marked selected rather than focused, and the skill treats that as the cursor. The same tools drive all three platforms, picked from the device id. It covers launching apps by bundle id, booting an Apple TV simulator or Android TV emulator, opening an Expo development build by deep link, and Fast Refresh, which needs a debug build and Metro started by the agent. For Fire TV it sends the agent to a separate reference file first, which uses the vega CLI to stop the Vega virtual device and set up Fast Refresh, and lists the JavaScript debugger tools that work there: logs, evaluation and network traffic, but not the component tree or the profilers.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/software-mansion/argent/tree/b965c94827d6167fd2912a7ca5ad5505040ae4e0/packages/skills/skills/argent-tv-interact"
        },
        "tags": [
          "category:debugging",
