      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Grants, denies or resets an app's runtime permissions on an iOS simulator or Android device through Argent, without the Settings UI.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "a test needs a permission such as camera, location or notifications set before the app asks, turned back on after a denial, or reset"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "edits the permission store directly: the iOS simulator's TCC database, or Android's runtime permissions over adb"
            },
            {
              "label": "Prefers",
              "text": "the app's own toggle or permission dialog whenever one can make the change, since that's the flow under test"
            },
            {
              "label": "Works with",
              "text": "11 runtime permissions, not all on both platforms, on iOS simulators and Android; not physical iPhones"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "the Argent MCP server"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Part of Software Mansion's Argent toolkit, which lets the agent control simulators, emulators and devices. Argent's settings-permissions tool is for test setup, not a general toggle, and this skill's table decides when to use it, first match winning: tap the app's own control or the system dialog when there is one; use the tool to grant or deny before launch, to turn back on a permission iOS won't ask for again, or to reset it so the first-run dialog returns. Anything outside the 11 runtime permissions, such as Wi-Fi or dark mode, goes through the Settings app or the app's own UI instead. Its gotchas cover the platform differences: on Android a pre-launch deny doesn't suppress the prompt, a reset below API 33 can't clear \"don't ask again\", and granting background location adds fine and coarse location too. Permissions are set before launching the app, since a change can terminate a running one.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/software-mansion/argent/tree/b965c94827d6167fd2912a7ca5ad5505040ae4e0/packages/skills/skills/argent-settings-permissions"
        },
