      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Converts Word, PowerPoint, Excel, OpenDocument, RTF, EPUB, CSV and PDF files to Markdown with Firecrawl's anydoc CLI so the agent can read them.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "the agent needs the contents of an office document, spreadsheet, presentation, ebook or PDF it can't read directly"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "runs npx @firecrawl/anydoc on the file, which detects the format from the file's content"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "GitHub-flavored Markdown, in the chat or written to a file the agent reads in parts"
            },
            {
              "label": "Scanned pages",
              "text": "anydoc does no OCR, so the agent reruns with --ocr hosted, which sends the document to Firecrawl Parse"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Node.js 20 or later; no install or signup, and an API key only for higher OCR limits"
            },
            {
              "label": "In code",
              "text": "inside a Node, Python or Rust project it uses the anydoc library instead of the CLI"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A short guide to anydoc, Firecrawl's document-to-Markdown converter. The agent runs it through npx, so nothing is installed, and gets Markdown on stdout; for a large document it writes to a file and reads only the parts it needs instead of pulling everything into context. It handles Word, PowerPoint and Excel files, old and new, their OpenDocument equivalents, RTF, EPUB, CSV and PDF. The format is detected from the file itself; the agent names it only for CSV on stdin or a missing or wrong extension. Exit codes tell it what happened: success, a document that couldn't be converted, a usage error, or PDF pages that need OCR. The CLI never prompts. Scanned and image-only pages can't be read locally, so the agent reruns with --ocr hosted, which uploads the document to Firecrawl Parse; no signup is needed, and a Firecrawl API key raises the limits.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/firecrawl/anydoc/tree/e7178e099b6bf9171e2c52b832cbdb4134b69112/skills/convert-documents-to-markdown"
        },
