              "text": "it falls back on its bundled craft guides and any references you give, with the same lock-and-ledger process"
            },
            {
              "label": "Wants to lead",
              "text": "it tells the agent not to use other design skills as a parallel authority, only for implementation details"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A research-first design method from Refero, a library of design references. Research is mandatory: the agent first writes a short brief, what is being designed, for whom, on which platform, the feeling and the main objection, then researches. Styles are design references extracted from real marketing and product pages, with tokens, typography, layout and do/don't rules; screens show how real products solve a specific UI problem; flows give the steps of journeys such as signup, checkout or cancellation. It studies several references and refuses to average them into a safe middle: one primary source sets mood, density and structure, others lend one or two details, and each token keeps its original role, so a CTA color stays CTA-only. That becomes a reference lock, a short list of traits to preserve, borrowed details, media strategy and defaults to reject. Work is routed by size: a direct build for small fixes, three reference-locked options to choose from for a redesign or landing page, an audit, or generated images only when needed. Its craft rules warn against current AI defaults, such as cream canvases with terracotta accents. A quality gate and a visual check against the lock come before handoff.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/referodesign/refero_skill/tree/2382e518f90096df607196b9a635da2d1bc142f9/skills/refero-design"
