      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Lets the agent work inside desktop apps such as Photoshop, Premiere, Blender, Unity and Office through Flue's scripting bridges.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you want the agent to inspect or edit a live document, scene or project inside a desktop app"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "sends small scripts into the app's own scripting runtime through a Flue bridge command and reads back JSON"
            },
            {
              "label": "Works with",
              "text": "Photoshop, Illustrator, InDesign, After Effects, Premiere, Audition, Blender, Unity, Houdini, 3ds Max, Word, Excel and PowerPoint"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "the Flue Python package and the app itself; the agent won't install Flue without your approval"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike an MCP server",
              "text": "it's plain shell commands, script in on stdin and JSON out, which Flue calls simpler; it still has a setup step and per-app quirks"
            },
            {
              "label": "Runs",
              "text": "as an entry point: after setup, Flue's installed skill and app-specific docs take over"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Coding agents can edit files and run shell commands but can't act inside a desktop application; Flue, a Python package, bridges that gap. For each app it has an adapter that passes a script from the shell into the app's own automation surface, such as ExtendScript for Adobe apps, bpy for Blender, Unity's editor APIs, COM or AppleScript, and returns the result or the error as JSON. The skill shows the pattern with a Photoshop script that draws three colored shapes as layers. It treats you as the driver: small, inspectable steps, nothing destructive unless you ask, real app state over guesses from training, and no unattended background work. This file is only the entry point. If Flue isn't on the machine, the agent says so and gives you the install command, but doesn't install it without your approval in that session; after setup, it follows Flue's installed skill and app docs.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/sfkislev/flue/tree/840bb1a3faaddc31689b7431a899038e2d1042ba/skills"
        },
