            {
              "label": "Unlike",
              "text": "a static scanner, it reports only what it could actually exploit"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The entry point to Strix, which runs AI pentesting agents that dynamically exploit a target and report only findings backed by a working proof-of-concept. Two interchangeable paths run the same engine: the open-source CLI, self-hosted in a Docker sandbox with your own LLM key, free and air-gap capable; and the managed app.strix.ai cloud, driven from the same binary with no Docker or key. The skill helps you choose per situation, then runs headless scans against local code, a deployed app or API, or a repo plus a live instance together, with scan modes from quick to deep and a budget cap. Results land in strix_runs as a report, per-finding files with PoCs, and SARIF. It warns that a clean exit is not proof of full coverage if a budget cap cut the run short. Hand findings to the fix skill and wire scanning into CI with the CI skill.",
