            },
            {
              "label": "Keeps",
              "text": "the fix verified by re-running the proof-of-concept, not just by inspection"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Turns validated Strix findings into minimal, correct fixes. It pulls findings from a local strix_runs report or the cloud, works critical-to-low, and, because every finding came with a proof-of-concept, re-tests rather than dismissing anything as a false positive. For each it fixes the root cause (parameterize every query, enforce authorization in the handler) and prefers the framework's built-in defense over ad-hoc sanitization, keeping the diff minimal. It then re-runs Strix scoped to the changed area, or replays the original PoC, to prove the issue is closed, and checks the run actually completed rather than stopping early on a budget cap. The report gives severity, root cause, fix location and verification result per finding, and flags that a leaked secret must be rotated, not just removed.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/usestrix/strix/tree/06015506625a78b981ae0b34be40239fc1b389be/skills/fix-security-vulnerabilities-with-strix"
