      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Adds Strix security scanning to CI/CD so every pull request gets a diff-scoped AI pentest that blocks vulnerable code before merge.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you want security scanning as a pre-merge gate in CI/CD"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "adds a diff-scoped Strix scan to the pipeline, or connects the managed PR-review app, that fails the build on validated findings"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "a workflow file or app connection, PR comments, and SARIF uploaded to code scanning"
            },
            {
              "label": "Works with",
              "text": "GitHub Actions, GitLab CI or any pipeline, self-hosted or managed"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Wires Strix into a pipeline two ways. The self-hosted option adds a workflow step that installs Strix and runs a quick diff-scoped scan of the PR's changed files in your runner's Docker, failing the build on exit code 2; it includes a guard that fails the job unless the run actually completed, since a budget-capped run can exit clean with partial coverage. The managed option connects the Strix GitHub/GitLab/Bitbucket app (or triggers from a pipeline via token) so PRs are reviewed with no runner, Docker or LLM key, results posting as PR comments and to a dashboard. Both emit SARIF 2.1.0 for code scanning, and the skill shows how to resolve the PR's real base branch for diff scope. It tells you which repository secrets to add rather than creating them.",
