      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Security-tests a REST, GraphQL or gRPC API with Strix, enumerating endpoints from a schema and exploiting the OWASP API Top 10 with proof-of-concept requests.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you want to security-test an API against the OWASP API Security Top 10"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "feeds Strix the OpenAPI/GraphQL/Postman schema and tokens, then exploits authorization, injection and resource-consumption flaws"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "a report with a proving request per finding, focused on BOLA/IDOR and function-level authorization"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "the Strix CLI or cloud; a schema and two tokens in different tenants matter most"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Targets the way APIs fail: no rendered surface to crawl, bugs that are authorization-shaped, and endpoints that behave differently per token. It collects what the agents need first, a schema (OpenAPI/Swagger or Postman as a direct target, a .proto or GraphQL endpoint otherwise), two tokens in different tenants to prove BOLA/IDOR, a low- and high-privilege token for function-level authorization, example object IDs, out-of-scope routes and any rate limits. It passes the spec as a target so agents start from the real endpoint list, runs the scan with a focus instruction mapped to the OWASP API Security Top 10 (2023), and can add the backend source for depth or reach internal APIs through the cloud's network connector. Each finding carries the exact request that proved it; replay it before reporting. Setup is in the penetration-testing skill; remediate with the fix skill and gate PRs with the CI skill.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/usestrix/strix/tree/06015506625a78b981ae0b34be40239fc1b389be/skills/api-security-testing"
