      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Audits a repo's CLAUDE.md files against a quality rubric, reports a grade for each, then applies the targeted fixes you approve.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you want to check whether your repo's CLAUDE.md files give Claude Code the project context it needs"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "finds every CLAUDE.md in the repo and scores each on commands, architecture, gotchas, conciseness, currency and actionability"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "a quality report with a score out of 100 and a letter grade per file, then the edits you approve, each shown as a diff"
            },
            {
              "label": "Keeps it minimal",
              "text": "adds commands, gotchas and quirks found in the code, not generic advice, obvious facts or one-off fixes"
            },
            {
              "label": "Asks first",
              "text": "always shows the report before proposing changes, and edits only after you confirm"
            }
          ],
          "text": "From Anthropic's claude-md-management plugin for Claude Code. CLAUDE.md is the file Claude Code reads for a project's context, such as build commands, structure and conventions; a repo can have one at its root, one per package or subfolder, and a personal .claude.local.md. The skill finds them all, then grades each against six weighted criteria: are build, test and deploy commands there, is the architecture clear, are non-obvious patterns documented, is it concise, does it match the current code, and are its instructions executable rather than vague. It flags stale commands, missing dependencies or environment setup, outdated structure and undocumented gotchas. Each proposed change names the file, shows the addition and says why it helps future sessions. With its recommendations it also passes on a few habits: the # key to have Claude add learnings to CLAUDE.md, .claude.local.md for personal settings kept out of git, and ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md for defaults across projects.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/anthropics/claude-plugins-official/tree/c07c748f1c680734a813eefd909bc073f8a9103f/plugins/claude-md-management/skills/claude-md-improver"
        },
